<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bahadur Shah Faruqi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 1596–1601</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bahadur Shah Faruqi was the last sultan of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khandesh">Khandesh</a> in the northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deccan">Deccan</a>. When he refused to submit to the Mughal emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akbar">Akbar</a>, Mughal armies besieged his great fortress of Asirgarh, which surrendered in January 1601. Bahadur Shah was imprisoned, and Khandesh was annexed as a Mughal province, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burhanpur">Burhanpur</a> becoming a base for Mughal campaigns in the Deccan.</p></div>
